  "description": "\tAPPLICATION FOR A LAWFUL DEVELOPMENT CERTIFICATE IN RESPECT OF THE PROPOSED CONVERSION OF A SINGLE DWELLINGHOUSE (C3) TO A SMALL HMO (HOUSE IN MULTIPLE OCCUPANCY) (C4) FOR UP TO 4 PERSONS",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The operations\r\nconsist of the use of 76 Claremont Avenue, New Malden, Surrey, Merton, KT3 6QN as\r\na small House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) under C4 Use&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt;mso-bidi-font-size:11.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Arial&quot;&gt;\r\nClass, in that the residential unit is used by three to six unrelated people.\r\nThe development constitutes permitted development within the meaning of Class\r\nL, of Part 3 of Schedule 2 to the Town &amp;amp; Country Planning (General\r\nPermitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) &quot;the Order&quot;\r\nand would comply with the development tolerances set out in said Class L. The\r\noperation would therefore have been granted planning permission by Article 3 of\r\nthe Order.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
